    category: "重大事件",
    title: "俄羅斯國家駭客Storm-2945攻擊旅館Wi-Fi，竊取Microsoft 365帳號與憑證",
    summary: "資安業者Microsoft揭露，俄羅斯國家級駭客Midnight Blizzard所屬的Storm-2945，自2026年5月起持續攻擊美國、印度、沙烏地等地的旅館及公共Wi-Fi網路。攻擊者透過竄改DNS組態與HTTP流量，將受害者導向惡意基礎架構，並使用假冒的更新頁面（ClickFix）誘騙使用者下載執行惡意程式。Storm-2945主要利用CornFlake木馬、ChocoShell竊資軟體，以及FruitStone控制面板，進行鍵盤側錄、螢幕截圖、監控，並竊取Microsoft 365的Cookie、密碼和登入權杖。此外，攻擊者甚至濫用Microsoft裝置驗證碼流程，誘導使用者在正常登入頁面輸入攻擊者提供的驗證碼，以取得OAuth權杖，進而控制帳號。Microsoft建議使用者在公共場所使用Wi-Fi時，應將其視為不可信任，避免存取敏感資料，並應使用加密通道。",
    tags: ["Storm-2945", "Microsoft 365", "公共Wi-Fi", "DNS竄改", "國家駭客", "OAuth權杖"],
    title_en: "Russian State Hacker Storm-2945 Attacks Hotel Wi-Fi, Steals Microsoft 365 Accounts and Credentials",
    summary_en: "Security firm Microsoft revealed that Storm-2945, affiliated with the Russian state-level hacker Midnight Blizzard, has been continuously attacking hotel and public Wi-Fi networks in the US, India, Saudi Arabia, and other regions since May 2026. The attackers manipulate DNS configurations and HTTP traffic to redirect victims to malicious infrastructure, and use fake update pages (ClickFix) to trick users into downloading and executing malware. Storm-2945 primarily utilizes the CornFlake backdoor, ChocoShell spyware, and FruitStone control panel to perform keylogging, screen capturing, and monitoring, thereby stealing Microsoft 365 cookies, passwords, and login tokens. Furthermore, the attackers even abused the Microsoft device verification process, tricking users into entering verification codes provided by the attackers on the normal login page to obtain OAuth tokens, thereby gaining control of the accounts. Microsoft advises users to treat public Wi-Fi as untrusted when in public places, avoid accessing sensitive data, and use encrypted channels.",
    tags_en: ["Storm-2945", "Microsoft 365", "Public Wi-Fi", "DNS Spoofing", "State Hacker", "OAuth Token"],
