    summary_en: "AerynOS announced the release of a new development version and ISO image, demonstrating the continued strong development of its Linux distribution. This update focuses on strengthening the core infrastructure, bringing users multiple practical improvements. Technically, the system has upgraded to the stable Linux 7.1 kernel, added experimental OpenZFS file system support, and includes continuously optimized Wayland integration. Furthermore, hardware support has been enhanced, notably with the integration of the NVIDIA R610 driver. On the software package front, updates include multiple versions such as the COSMIC 1.5 desktop environment, KDE Plasma 6.7.3, PHP 8.5.9, QEMU 11.0.3, and Wine 11.14. Developers continue to optimize the build and package toolchain to provide a more stable Linux distribution experience. Users can download the latest version from the official AerynOS blog.",
