    category: "漏洞與威脅情報",
    title: "CISA新增CVE-2026-18577至已知漏洞目錄，警告N-able N-central認證繞過風險",
    summary: "美國網路安全局（CISA）宣布將一個新的已知被利用漏洞（KEV）加入其目錄，該漏洞為CVE-2026-18577，影響N-able N-central產品，屬於認證繞過（Authentication Bypass）類型。此類漏洞是惡意網路行為者常用的攻擊途徑，對企業系統構成重大風險。CISA的《約束性營運指令》（BOD 26-04）已要求聯邦政府機構必須優先修補KEV目錄中的高風險漏洞，特別是那些在公開暴露資產上可授予完全控制權的漏洞。雖然此指令僅適用於聯邦政府，但CISA鼓勵所有組織應採納風險導向的漏洞管理策略，將修補KEV目錄中的漏洞列為最高優先級。建議所有使用N-able N-central的組織，應立即關注並修補此類已知的、被積極利用的漏洞。",
    tags: ["CISA", "KEV Catalog", "CVE-2026-18577", "N-able N-central", "認證繞過", "漏洞管理"],
    title_en: "CISA Adds CVE-2026-18577 to Known Exploited Vulnerabilities Catalog, Warning N-able N-central Authentication Bypass Risk",
    summary_en: "The U.S. Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA) announced the addition of a new Known Exploited Vulnerability (KEV) to its catalog: CVE-2026-18577. This vulnerability affects N-able N-central and is classified as an Authentication Bypass type. This type of vulnerability is a common attack vector used by malicious actors, posing a significant risk to enterprise systems. CISA's Binding Operational Directive (BOD 26-04) requires federal government agencies to prioritize patching high-risk vulnerabilities listed in the KEV catalog, especially those that can grant full control over publicly exposed assets. Although this directive only applies to federal government entities, CISA encourages all organizations to adopt a risk-based vulnerability management strategy, listing the patching of KEV catalog vulnerabilities as the highest priority. All organizations using N-able N-central are advised to immediately pay attention to and patch this known, actively exploited vulnerability.",
    tags_en: ["CISA", "KEV Catalog", "CVE-2026-18577", "N-able N-central", "Authentication Bypass", "Vulnerability Management"],
